{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And she shall be purified from the source of her blood.</b> What does it say? For even during all the days of purity her blood is pure, and even if you say it refers to blood of impurity — in any case it should not have mentioned blood, for the matter does not depend on blood, since even in a dry birth she is impure. And one may answer that this is what it says: 'and she shall be purified' — from the law of the source of her blood, whose law is to be impure. And even though we hold that regarding blood of purity the expression 'and she shall be purified' is applicable, because she was not eating terumah and consecrated foods."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:00.010844041Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}